## Model Summary

This model card provides DPA3 models[1] trained on the SPICE-MACE-OFF[2] datasets. We provide four models with the following configurations:

- `DPA3-L3` – 3 layers, smallest and fastest variant
- `DPA3-L6` – 6 layers, accuracy–efficiency sweet spot
- `DPA3-L12` – 12 layers, higher accuracy
- `DPA3-L24` – 24 layers, highest accuracy among DPA3 models

All models are compatible with **DeePMD-kit v3.1.0**. For other installation options, please visit the [Releases page](https://github.com/deepmodeling/deepmd-kit/releases/tag/v3.1.0) page to download the off-line package for v3.1.0**, and refer to the [official documentation](https://docs.deepmodeling.com/projects/deepmd/en/v3.0.0/install/easy-install.html) for off-line installation instructions.

## Usage

### Model Evaluation

Evaluate the models through the dp test command line:

```bash
dp --pt test -m DPA3-L6.pt -s path_to_your_system
```

### ASE Calculator

You can directly use the following Python code for prediction or optimization with standard ASE calculator:

```python
## Compute potential energy
from ase import Atoms
from deepmd.calculator import DP as DPCalculator
dp = DPCalculator("DPA3-L6.pt")
water = Atoms('H2O', positions=[(0.7601, 1.9270, 1), (1.9575, 1, 1), (1., 1., 1.)], cell=[100, 100, 100])
water.calc = dp
print(water.get_potential_energy())
print(water.get_forces())

## Run BFGS structure optimization
from ase.optimize import BFGS
dyn = BFGS(water)
dyn.run(fmax=1e-6)
print(water.get_positions())
```

### LAMMPS

Use LAMMPS for molecular dynamics calculation with DPA3 models, you first need to freeze the *.pt models into *.pth models use the following command:

```bash
dp --pt freeze -c DPA3-L6.pt -o DPA3-L6.pth
```

Then you can make the following modifications in the LAMMPS script to call the DeePMD-kit interface (also see `potential.md`):

```bash
pair_style      deepmd DPA3-L6.pth
# If atom names (O H in this example) are not set in the pair_coeff command, the type_map defined by the training parameter will be used by default.
pair_coeff      * * O H
```

## Training Dataset

The models are trained on the **SPICE-MACE-OFF** dataset. This small-molecule dataset, originally developed for training the **MACE-OFF23** model, combines:

- 85% of the SPICE v1 subset, consisting of neutral molecules containing
  H, C, N, O, F, P, S, Cl, Br, and I
- Geometries from classical MD simulations at 300 K and 500 K, providing diverse conformations for molecules with ≤ 50 atoms

The dataset is further extended to larger systems via:

- GFN2-xTB MD–generated molecules with 50–90 atoms, derived from QMugs
- Water clusters (up to 50 molecules) extracted from liquid water MD trajectories

All energies and forces are computed at the
ωB97M-D3(BJ)/def2-TZVPPD level of theory using PSI4.

Data splitting is performed at the molecule level to avoid conformation leakage between sets:

- 95% of the data (951,005 structures) is used for training/validation
- 5% of the data (50,195 structures) is used for testing

Additional test cases include COMP6 tripeptides recomputed at the SPICE level of theory. However, because these tripeptides are not present in the SPICE-MACE-OFF test split, quantitative accuracy comparisons are restricted to the remaining molecular systems.

---

## Training Details

We train the **DPA3** models in four depth configurations with 3, 6, 12, and 24 layers. All configurations are truncated within LiGS order 2.

### Training setup

- **Engine:** DeePMD-kit (`v3.1.0` required)
- **Batch size:** `auto:256` (DeePMD-kit automatic batchsize)
- **Hardware:** 8 × GPU cards
- **Training schedule:**
  - Two rounds of training
  - Each round: **4 million steps**
- **Cutoff radii:**
  - `e_rcut = 6.0`
  - `a_rcut = 4.0`

Other hyperparameters and training details can be found in DPA3 paper[1].

---

## 3. Performance

### 3.1 Accuracy

Compared to baseline models, DPA3 demonstrates strong accuracy on both the SPICE-MACE-OFF test set and the TorsionNet500 benchmark:

<p align="center">
  <img src="https://store-cn.aissquare.com/markdown/models/3a88b973-6780-4291-9cd3-9f01812ef9f5/spice.png"
       alt="spice"
       style="width:50%;">
</p>

<p align="center">
  <img src="https://store-cn.aissquare.com/markdown/models/5ed73749-8a1a-463e-a38b-858262ef2afc/torsion.png"
       alt="torsion"
       style="width:50%;">
</p>

Key observations on SPICE-MACE-OFF test set:

- **DPA3-L3**

  - Achieves **comparable energy logarithmic-weighted average MAE (LWAMAE)** to **MACE(M)**
  - Uses only **~40%** of the parameters: **0.9M** vs **2.3M** for MACE(M)
- **DPA3-L6**

  - Achieves approximately **34% lower energy LWAMAE** than **MACE(L)**
  - Uses only **~20%** of the parameters: **1.3M** vs **6.9M** for MACE(L)
- **DPA3-L24**

  - Significantly outperforms **MACE(L)**
  - Reduces **energy LWAMAE by ~66%**
  - Still uses **~30% fewer parameters**: **4.9M** vs **6.9M** for MACE(L)

